A||||16||fierospeeder||HID blinding headlights||||1||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-16-2001||02:03 AM||||on the nbc news today (monday at 10pm), they had one guy from illinois who was ticketed for driving with hid headlights.  He owns a Audi with the new lights.  The ticket states "blue lights".  <P>The person believes hes not at fault because his car came with HID from the factory.  He got the ticket dismissed at court.  <P>The headlight thing is suppose to be discussed at the nhs_?  So you can post your opinions on their website.  There is a link on the  <A HREF="http://www.nbc5.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nbc5.com</A>  website.  <P>A lot of people dislike the bright beams and they do cause destractions.  Some complained of headaches.  <P>I personally hate them, and other headlights that dont have any diffusion on the lenses.  It is dangerous to be blinded at night for a second.  Even a second, an accident can happen.  <P>I also hate day time running lights.  There are some cars that seem to have their brights on.  Parking lights is something more preferable.  I understand that emergency vehicles use their headlights, and motorcycles need their headlights for other drivers to see them.  Unlike a car which is a lot larger in size.  If you hit a car then your a moron if you didn't see it.  Its a law in illinois that your lights need to be on when it rains and your wipers are on.  This is the only time i would accept lights besides funerals and night driving.  <P>Poseurs that pretend to have daytime running lights is really lame when you can see their tail lights on.  Just like putting stickers on your car to make it go faster.<P><BR>I thought i would be like the news broadcast and state this at the end.  The guy was pulled over and ticketed also for an improper or missing license plate.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jaei Sun||10-16-2001||12:51 PM||||I love em personally, the light output for the driver of the vehicle with them is fantastic!  Lights things up like it was daylight out.<P>In the future I plan on getting them as long as the law will allow.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||falconhulk||10-16-2001||01:15 PM||||see no problem with it either.  Day time running lights dont bother me a bit either.  Thats like saying a persons air freshner is gettin on your nerves.  Headlights cant blind you during the day.  I think someone needs to spend more time watching the road in front of him then to the left.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||10-16-2001||02:46 PM||||None of the old cars with their brights on are bright enough in the daylight.  But the new cars have headlights that can be blinding.  And their are probably people that turn on their brights accidentaly or for road rage.<P>I guess the sun isn't bright enough during daylight either to blind someone?  If your stating its impossible for a source of light to be blinding.  Visors should be removed from cars, unless makeup is needed to be applied.  There is different intensities of light. All of them have different effects on the human body.  Light is composed of photon particles and wavelengths.  Certain wavelengths do more damage then others.  <P>I can also say, if you need to upgrade your lighting system because the manufactured that supplied it on the car isn't emitting enough light then you need to stay off the road because your blind and an usafe driver.  Or your speeding because your driving to fast to respond to the reflection of light hitting the objects and getting back to your eye.||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||10-16-2001||03:45 PM||||heh heh heh heh.  The sun is a lot more powerful then headlights. Also its the wavelength of the light from the sun thats the problem.  I can safely state I have looked straight at HID lights during the day without even squinting.  Now of course it was from the next lane.  I did not run up and touch my nose to the headlight, as this might produce the blinding effect you speak of.  lol!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||10-16-2001||04:32 PM||||I have seen reports on the HID lights being blinding too.... with some interesting reason that may answer the "why".<P>Of course, there is the usual suspects... misalignment.  Althought that probably isn't the cause of all the complaints.<P>The one I thought was interesting was that people just aren't used to them!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Cars in Europe have used HID lights for years without complaint.  Also, when Halogen lights first came onto the market... everyone was used to the incandescent bulbs and felt the new halogen ones should be banned for being blinding and dangerous too.<P>Maybe its all a matter of more of them coming onto the market so people aren't so surprised by their brightness.  They sure are nice when your trying to see on those country back roads at night!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-16-2001||05:46 PM||||a little off topic but I have both on mine, i only use the brite ones out of town in the boonies. Last week I passed a guy doing 45 in a 55 zone on my low lites. It was a straight stretch of 2 lane for several miles. He was driving an Explorer and acted like I did something terrible to him and ran right up on my back bumper with his brite lites in my mirror. I just flipped the dimmer. He stayed there for prob 2 miles. I finally brake checked him hard. Then he saw the light after eating his steering wheel. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||10-16-2001||06:09 PM||||I did that once, and the fncking moron put his blazer into a spinout!<P>For a split-second, I almost considered feeling like a ham  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"Duct Tape is Good to Mach 3"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smileystooges.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/totalsmash.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/space_cowboy_hat.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smashfreakB.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smileystooges.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/sa38.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||fierospeeder||10-16-2001||06:21 PM||||typical SUV driver.<P><BR>i totally hate people that do that.  My friend and i were going to Indy 500 and were driving at about the time of 2am.  He was driving his truck, Those jeeps with the wooden panels on the side, i cant remember what the name of the truck is.<P>So we were driving perfectly fine, in the middle lane and we get a economy car get on our ass and puts on his brights for no particular reason.  He passes us after 5 minutes and slows down.<P>My g/f was driving her sisters truck.  We were going to the casino, (something she likes to do), and someone cuts us off.  She flicks her brights on/off for a sec.  Later on, cause of traffic, the car/suv got behind us and they were on our ass with their brights on.<P><BR>There are a lot of people in illinois with misaligned headlights.  Sometimes theres one that goes straight ahead and the other is pointing up.  And theres the people that have no operational brake lights at all.<BR>Some people are so considerete of others and leave their headlights off at night not too blind oncoming traffic.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||10-17-2001||10:58 PM||||I almost allways turn on the lights when driving any car(except my fiero). Even during the day. I hope people notice me coming, allot of idiots out driving and the last thing I want is someone not seing me when im on the road.<P>My old 88 coupe had extra bright headlamps in it. I forget what kind they were. But I often got flashed because people thought I had on my highbeams!<P>What I really love on import cars are the passing lights. Lets you flash the low and high beams at the same time. On the SAAB I often drive I can have low beam,highbeam,and the fogs on all at one time. People tend to move the hell out of the left lane when you have this many watts shining in there rear view, let alone when they are all flashing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 10-17-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||fierospeeder||10-17-2001||11:03 PM||||heres a link to the newsgroup that had a flame ware about day time running lights.<BR>A lot of motorcyclists (me) did flame about it because it doesn't make motorcycles any obvious then any other vehicle with their headlights on.<BR> <A HREF="http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&threadm=73da2590.0110170638.36bd09f2%40posting.google.com&prev=/groups%3Fhl%3Den%26group%3Drec.autos.driving" TARGET=_blank>http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&threadm=73da2590.0110170638.36bd09f2%40posting.google.com&prev=/groups%3Fhl%3Den%26group%3Drec.autos.driving</A> <P>Heres another link to a flame war about HID and bright lights causing glare.http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&threadm=Pine.SOL.4.33.0110171322280.24883-100000%40azure.engin.umich.edu&prev=/groups%3Fhl%3Den%26group%3Drec.autos.driving<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierospeeder||10-17-2001||11:04 PM||||DOH!!<BR> <A HREF="http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&threadm=Pine.SOL.4.33.0110171322280.24883-100000%40azure.engin.umich.edu&prev=/groups%3Fhl%3Den%26group%3Drec.autos.driving" TARGET=_blank>http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&threadm=Pine.SOL.4.33.0110171322280.24883-100000%40azure.engin.umich.edu&prev=/groups%3Fhl%3Den%26group%3Drec.autos.driving</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||10-19-2001||01:26 AM||||I have HID lights on my fiero.<P>All I have to say is that any technological advancement is met with resistance by the ignorant masses, and those who are threatened by it's existance.<P>If a cop ever tickets me, I will not just fight the ticket, but file harasement suits, and a criminal endangerment suits against both the state of the ticket, and against the ticketing officer.<P>Trying to GET ME ****ING KILLED by removing what I find an essential safety feature of my car? Come get some.<P>Yes, I am the ass with the 'blue lights' and I'll not only take you to a DOT testing facuility to prove they're legal in brightneess and pattern, but make you pay for it.<P>While the guy with (any) Ford truck with plain 'ol hick lights blinds everyone he sees.<P>HID lights are roughly the wavelegnth of moon and (of course) sunlight.  They are no brighter, but more reflected light comes back due to the above.<P>People who are 'blinded' by them are morons, plain and simple.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||Leper||10-19-2001||04:15 AM||||I'd take a set of HID headlights in a second if I could afford them. The stock Fiero (or any other car's that I've seen) halogens suck.<P>They had this story on the news (Not the Audi one, that's actually a different story altogether, about an ignorant cop. The person wasn't at fault because he didn't have the illegal poser blue headlights. The guy wrote to Motor trend or Car and Driver to make sure and the letter was put in the magazine.) <BR>The news report stated that the government isn't going to ban HID lights. They are thinking about making auto dimming mirrors standard on future cars to keep people from being blinded. While that makes sense, it doesn't do anything about the lights of oncoming traffic.<P> I do have a problem with being temporarily blinded by other peoples headlights, but it's not neccisarily cars with HID lights doing it. Ford F series 4x4's are the worst. Apparantly their headlights are aimed pretty much where my eyes like to be when I'm driving my car. The 2x4's are lower and don't seem to do it as much. My friends 97 4x4 doesn't even shine that much light on the road, the driving lights do most of the work.||||reg||1
Z||000014||ChopTop||10-19-2001||10:31 AM||||Another issue that needs to be mentioned is while HIDs may not blind you when your in your 20s they may when you're in your 40s.  The older you get the slower you eyes respond to brightness.  Technology is great, but that doesn't mean you shouldn't be concerned with the impact new technology causes.  As of now I don't have a problem with HID, I'd like a set on my cars.  I have more problems with the height of vehicles.  But there isn't anything I can do about that since my car sits so low.  But I would like to install a see through mirror in my back window so that when SUVs try to see how close they can get to the rear of my car they will get a taste of what it feels like to be blinded.||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||10-20-2001||03:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>I'd take a set of HID headlights in a second if I could afford them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The good news is: They're getting cheaper!!!<P>$5,000... $3,000... $2,000....(on new cars)   $5-600 in aftermarket kits or so right now...  and you can find them (only a little) cheaper if you really hunt.<P>Lots of the cost is in the Ballast, so I don't see them ever droping much below ~$150 in aftermarket kits for both lights... (this won't occur for several (5-10) years, at which time I belive the DOT in the US at least will actually require discharge lighting... as they essentially do now Halogens.<P>But that's got to be only about twice what 'OEM' replacement fiero lights would cost if you were to actually purchase them from a GM dealer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
